data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JBT6bFt4VoxNSSZSCZhg7q","output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: financial-analysis\n     3\tdescription: >\n     4\t  Analyze Techcombank financial performance data: variance analysis, trend\n     5\t  identification, achievement tracking, and cross-segment comparison using\n     6\t  inline arithmetic (show working), markdown tables, and knowledge base\n     7\t  retrieval tools.\n     8\t\n     9\t  TRIGGER when the user asks to analyze, compare, or compute financial metrics\n    10\t  such as TOI, NII, NFI, NIM, CASA, OPEX, CIR, or any banking performance\n    11\t  indicator. Also trigger for: actual vs budget, YoY comparison, variance\n    12\t  analysis, achievement rate, segment comparison (RBG vs CIBG), trend analysis\n    13\t  on financial data, or questions about business terminology / segmentation.\n    14\t\n    15\t  DO NOT TRIGGER for: general data questions without financial metrics,\n    16\t  dashboard creation (use databricks-dashboard), or report formatting only\n    17\t  (use report-writer).\n    18\t---\n    19\t\n    20\t# Financial Analysis Skill\n    21\t\n    22\t## Overview\n    23\t\n    24\tThis skill provides frameworks for analyzing Techcombank financial performance\n    25\tdata. It covers metric definitions, analysis workflows, temporal resolution,\n    26\tinline arithmetic with explicit formulas, and business context retrieval from\n    27\tthe knowledge base.\n    28\t\n    29\t## Workflow\n    30\t\n    31\t```\n    32\tUser question\n    33\t    ↓\n    34\t1. Retrieve business context if needed (→ Knowledge Base Retrieval below)\n    35\t    ↓\n    36\t2. Resolve temporal references (→ analysis_frameworks.md §6)\n    37\t    ↓\n    38\t3. Identify metrics and segments (→ metrics_glossary.md + KB context)\n    39\t    ↓\n    40\t4. Delegate to sub-agents (English, absolute dates)\n    41\t    ↓\n    42\t5. Compute derived metrics inline — show formula (→ tool_reference.md §1)\n    43\t    ↓\n    44\t6. Present results in markdown tables with units and bold key numbers\n    45\t    ↓\n    46\t7. Generate action recommendations (→ /skills/action-recommendation/SKILL.md)\n    47\t   - Grep wiki for campaigns, products, policies relevant to identified gaps\n    48\t   - Combine with LLM banking expertise for concrete next steps\n    49\t    ↓\n    50\t8. Write analysis (findings + attribution + actions)\n    51\t```\n    52\t\n    53\t## Quick Decision Tree\n    54\t\n    55\t| User intent | Framework | Reference |\n    56\t|---|---|---|\n    57\t| \"TOI actual vs budget\" | Variance Analysis | `analysis_frameworks.md` §1 |\n    58\t| \"NII trend 2024\" | Trend Analysis | `analysis_frameworks.md` §2 |\n    59\t| \"Achievement rate RBG\" | Achievement Analysis | `analysis_frameworks.md` §3 |\n    60\t| \"Compare RBG vs CIBG\" | Cross-Segment | `analysis_frameworks.md` §4 |\n    61\t| \"TOI tháng trước\" | Temporal Resolution | `analysis_frameworks.md` §6 |\n    62\t| \"What is NIM?\" | Metric Definition | `metrics_glossary.md` §1 or KB |\n    63\t| How to compute metrics | Inline Formulas | `tool_reference.md` §1 |\n    64\t| How to build tables | Markdown Tables | `tool_reference.md` §1 (Presentation Rules) |\n    65\t| Customer segmentation, product hierarchy | Business Knowledge | KB retrieval tools |\n    66\t\n    67\t## Knowledge Base Retrieval\n    68\t\n    69\tThe agent has access to pre-indexed business knowledge documents via 3 tools.\n    70\tUse these to ground analysis in accurate business terminology and context.\n    71\t\n    72\t### When to Retrieve\n    73\t\n    74\t- User asks about customer segmentation (Mass, Emerging Affluent, Affluent, HNW)\n    75\t- User asks about product hierarchy or P&L framework\n    76\t- Before analyzing data that involves specific segments, tiers, or personas\n    77\t- When you need precise definitions beyond what `metrics_glossary.md` covers\n    78\t- Before delegating to `dashboard_agent` — include relevant context as `<business_context>`\n    79\t\n    80\t### How to Retrieve\n    81\t\n    82\t```\n    83\tlist_knowledge_docs()              → see available documents\n    84\tget_knowledge_structure(doc_id)    → browse TOC, find relevant sections\n    85\tget_knowledge_content(doc_id, \"45-80\")  → fetch specific section text\n    86\t```\n    87\t\n    88\t**Tip:** Start with `get_knowledge_structure` to find the right section line\n    89\tnumbers, then call `get_knowledge_content` with a targeted range. Avoid\n    90\tretrieving the entire document.\n    91\t\n    92\t## Key Rules\n    93\t\n    94\t1. **Show arithmetic working** — write formulas explicitly for all derived values\n    95\t2. **Never fabricate data** — every number must come from a sub-agent result\n    96\t3. **Never rescale values** — sub-agent data is already in display units (tỷ VND, %, count). NEVER divide (`/1000`, `/1M`, `/1B`) or multiply (`*100`). This produces wrong values (often 0.00). Use values **exactly as returned**.\n    97\t4. **Resolve all temporal references** before delegating to sub-agents\n    98\t5. **Additive vs Rate metrics** — never sum rate metrics (NIM, CASA, CIR)\n    99\t6. **Same period, same scenario** for fair cross-segment comparisons\n   100\t7. **Use markdown tables** for any structured data with 3+ rows","duration_ms":0}}

