data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_016Gk1duZmmb7aruhtcNomr8","output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: action-recommendation\n     3\tdescription: >-\n     4\t  Generate concrete, prioritized action recommendations from financial insights.\n     5\t  ALWAYS included as the final step of every data analysis and report output.\n     6\t  Combines wiki knowledge (campaigns, products, pricing) with LLM banking\n     7\t  expertise to produce specific next-step actions grounded in data evidence.\n     8\t  Actions MUST pass the Relevance Test — only include actions that directly\n     9\t  move the underperforming metric for the exact segment/product being analyzed.\n    10\t---\n    11\t\n    12\t## Core Principle: Direct Causality\n    13\t\n    14\tEvery action must have a **direct causal path** to the metric gap identified. \"Direct\" = the action moves the metric within 1 logical step, no intermediary assumptions.\n    15\t\n    16\tTest: if the CEO asks \"how does this action fix the problem we just discussed?\", the answer must be immediate and obvious — not \"if X then Y then Z\".\n    17\t\n    18\t## Workflow\n    19\t\n    20\t1. **Identify gaps** — which metrics underperform, by how much, which segments drag\n    21\t2. **Define scope boundary** — lock segment, product, geography, time period. Actions MUST stay within this boundary.\n    22\t3. **Relevance Test** (MANDATORY) — `read_file` → `references/relevance-test.md`. Every candidate action passes 3 gates.\n    23\t4. **Wiki lookup** (conditional) — search wiki matching gap AND scope. Skip wiki content targeting different segments.\n    24\t5. **Synthesize** — filtered context + banking expertise → 3–5 concrete actions\n    25\t6. **Evaluate & Score** — `read_file` → `references/evaluation-criteria.md`. Score 5 dimensions, apply elimination rules.\n    26\t7. **Market enrichment** (TRY) — `read_file` → `skills/market-intelligence/SKILL.md`. For each action, map metric gap → topic in query-catalog.md, call `web_search`, inject `market_signal` into Why field. If unavailable/disabled: skip silently, keep actions as-is.\n    27\t8. **Format** — per template below\n    28\t\n    29\t## References (read on demand)\n    30\t\n    31\t| File | When to read | Content |\n    32\t| --- | --- | --- |\n    33\t| `references/relevance-test.md` | Step 3: before including any action | 3 Gates, Causal Chain, Wiki decision tree |\n    34\t| `references/evaluation-criteria.md` | Step 6: after generating candidates | 5-dimension rubric, scoring guide, priority formula |\n    35\t| `references/anti-patterns.md` | When unsure if action belongs | 4 anti-patterns with wrong/right examples, scope-locked pattern |\n    36\t| `skills/market-intelligence/SKILL.md` | Action generation: market signal enrichment | When/how to call web_search, interpret results, inject signals |\n    37\t| `skills/market-intelligence/query-catalog.md` | Action generation: query selection | Topic-to-query mapping, domains, recency windows |\n    38\t\n    39\t## Action Format\n    40\t\n    41\t```\n    42\t**🔴/🟡/🟢 [Priority] Action Title**\n    43\t- Why: Data evidence (exact metric/gap + root cause)\n    44\t  📡 Market Signal: <key_signal from web_search> (optional, only when available)\n    45\t- Action: Specific steps (1-3 concrete actions)\n    46\t- Impact: Quantified metric improvement (direct path only)\n    47\t- Owner: Team/role responsible\n    48\t```\n    49\t\n    50\t## Priority Levels\n    51\t\n    52\t- 🔴 **High** — Impact >30% gap, feasible now, 1-step causal chain within same segment\n    53\t- 🟡 **Medium** — 10-30% gap closure, needs coordination, still direct\n    54\t- 🟢 **Long-term** — <10% or cross-functional dependency (rare — most should be 🔴/🟡)\n    55\t\n    56\t**Hard rule:** Directness=1 (multi-step or different scope) → can NEVER be 🔴.\n    57\t\n    58\t## Rules\n    59\t\n    60\t1. **Relevance Test first** — every action passes 3 gates before formatting\n    61\t2. **Scope-locked** — actions stay within the segment/product/geography being analyzed\n    62\t3. **Ground in data** — every action cites the specific metric/gap from the analysis\n    63\t4. **Wiki conditional** — only reference wiki content matching scope boundary\n    64\t5. **Be concrete** — BAD: \"Increase CASA\". GOOD: \"CASA payroll for HH customers earning ≥30M, target +20K B in Q3\"\n    65\t6. **Max 5 actions** — highest-leverage, scope-matched, ordered by priority\n    66\t7. **Match user language** — Vietnamese query → Vietnamese actions; English query → English actions\n    67\t8. **No borrowed campaigns** — campaign targets different segment → do NOT include, even \"adapted\"\n    68\t9. **Cross-segment insights** → separate \"Additional Notes\" section (NOT in action list)\n    69\t\n    70\t## HTML Report Integration\n    71\t\n    72\tPlacement: `SECTIONS → ... → ACTIONS → FOOTER`\n    73\t\n    74\tUses: priority badges (🔴/🟡/🟢) · card layout (Why/Action/Impact/Owner) · collapsible details\n    75\t","duration_ms":0}}

