data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_011u5AQNhSYNLu4sprcN4W5t","output":"     1\t---\n     2\tname: report-builder-v2\n     3\tdescription: Builds an interactive, filterable HTML report (PowerBI-style) from a compact JSON ReportConfig via the build_report tool. Use when the user asks for a report, a báo cáo, an executive summary as a document, a dashboard-style HTML deliverable, or a shareable link to analysis results.\n     4\t---\n     5\t\n     6\t# Report Builder v2\n     7\t\n     8\tYou write a **JSON `ReportConfig`**; `build_report` renders it into a self-contained\n     9\tinteractive report (sidebar, slicers, cross-filtering charts, RAG, sortable tables,\n    10\tlight/dark themes). The template owns all HTML/CSS/JS and every color — you never write\n    11\tmarkup and never choose a theme. Your job is content, data and relationships.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Workflow\n    14\t\n    15\t1. **Open a preset in `assets/examples/` and read it fully** — it is your template.\n    16\t   - `performance.json` — segment P&L. Wide facts (one row per sector, `actual`/`budget`\n    17\t     as columns), one slicer, `insight` · `subtitle` · `kpi_group` · `driver_row` ·\n    18\t     `chart` · `chart_pair` · `table` (fact-driven) · `actions`, RAG.\n    19\t   - `campaign.json` — marketing. Adds `divider`, an `afb_line` with `forecast_band`, and\n    20\t     a `table` in explicit `rows` mode for hand-curated cells.\n    21\t   - `segment_scenario.json` — long facts (`scenario` column: Actual/Budget/SPLY) with a\n    22\t     declaration-only dimension. Copy this one whenever your data has a scenario or\n    23\t     metric column rather than one column per scenario.\n    24\t2. **Paste the sub-agent's numbers into `data.facts` verbatim.** Display units, as returned.\n    25\t3. **Declare a measure for every figure you will show**, then bind them with `{{measure}}`.\n    26\t4. **Write the config with `write_file` to `/report_config.json`, then call\n    27\t   `build_report(config_path=\"/report_config.json\", filename=…)`.**\n    28\t\n    29\tAdapt the preset and send it. `build_report` validates before rendering and returns\n    30\t**every** problem it found in one message, each with its location — so submitting a config\n    31\tis how you check it. Re-reading your own JSON to be certain first costs more than the call\n    32\tdoes, and finds less.\n    33\t\n    34\tOn an `ERROR:` return, patch with `edit_file` on the same file (not a full rewrite) and\n    35\tcall `build_report` again with the same `config_path`. Read the errors literally and group\n    36\tthem: `where clause points at an undeclared dimension: 'scenario'` repeated across 13\n    37\tmeasures is one missing declaration in `data.dimensions` — *undeclared* means **add** the\n    38\tdeclaration, never delete the reference. `edit_file`'s `old_string` must match the file as\n    39\tit stands right now.\n    40\t\n    41\tOn success you get a link; the HTML and its source config JSON are saved side by side.\n    42\t\n    43\t## Config shape\n    44\t\n    45\t```\n    46\t{ \"meta\": {...}, \"data\": { \"dimensions\": {...}, \"facts\": {...} },\n    47\t  \"measures\": {...}, \"filters\": [...], \"conditional_formats\": {...}, \"sections\": [...] }\n    48\t```\n    49\t\n    50\t`meta`, `data`, `sections` required. Full contract:\n    51\t`contracts/report-config.schema.json`. Semantics: `.specify/specs/001-report-builder-v2/data-model.md`.\n    52\t\n    53\t## Data\n    54\t\n    55\t`data.facts` maps `fact_id → [row, …]`. A column named like a declared dimension is a\n    56\tdimension reference; other numeric columns are measurable.\n    57\t\n    58\t**Every categorical column you reference must be declared in `data.dimensions`** — in a\n    59\tmeasure `where`, as a chart axis, as a table `dim` — with a `keys` entry for each value in\n    60\tthe rows. That includes query-only columns like `scenario` (Actual/Budget/SPLY) or `metric`\n    61\t(CASA/Lending/AUM) which you never expose to the user: declaring a dimension does not\n    62\tcreate a slicer, only `filters[]` does.\n    63\t\n    64\t```json\n    65\t\"dimensions\": {\n    66\t  \"sector\":   { \"label\": \"Sector\", \"keys\": [\n    67\t      { \"key\": \"re\", \"label\": \"Real Estate\" }, { \"key\": \"infra\", \"label\": \"Infrastructure\" } ] },\n    68\t  \"scenario\": { \"label\": \"Kịch bản\", \"keys\": [\n    69\t      { \"key\": \"Actual\", \"label\": \"Thực tế\" }, { \"key\": \"Budget\", \"label\": \"Kế hoạch\" } ] }\n    70\t},\n    71\t\"facts\": { \"sector_pnl\": [\n    72\t    { \"sector\": \"re\", \"scenario\": \"Actual\", \"toi\": 4349.8, \"nii\": 2383.7, \"nfi\": 1966.1 },\n    73\t    { \"sector\": \"re\", \"scenario\": \"Budget\", \"toi\": 4716.5, \"nii\": 2502.0, \"nfi\": 2101.2 } ] }\n    74\t```\n    75\t\n    76\t`sector` also goes in `filters[]` (a slicer); `scenario` stays declaration-only.\n    77\t\n    78\t## Measures\n    79\t\n    80\tEvery displayed number comes from a measure — exactly **one** kind per measure, since the\n    81\tschema branches are `additionalProperties:false` and a mixed measure fails all three as a\n    82\tcryptic shape error.\n    83\t\n    84\t| Kind | Shape | Reacts to filter? |\n    85\t|------|-------|-------------------|\n    86\t| aggregate | `{ \"agg\": \"sum\\|avg\\|min\\|max\\|count\\|last\\|first\", \"fact\": \"…\", \"col\": \"…\", \"where\": {…}? }` | yes — recomputed over active rows |\n    87\t| expr | `{ \"expr\": \"toi_act / toi_bud * 100\" }` (arithmetic over other measures only) | yes |\n    88\t| const | `{ \"const\": 10973 }` (a scalar the sub-agent returned) | no |\n    89\t\n    90\t`where` pins an aggregate to fixed rows regardless of slicer state:\n    91\t`{\"scenario\": \"Actual\"}`, `{\"sector\": [\"re\",\"infra\"]}`. Its columns and values must be\n    92\tdeclared dimensions and declared keys.\n    93\t\n    94\t`\"format\"` sets display only — `ty0 ty1 ty2` (10.973 / 4.349,8), `pct1` (94,8%),\n    95\t`signed_ty1` (+779,7 / −288), `usd_mn`, `kh`. Formatting never rescales.\n    96\t\n    97\t### Every figure is a token (Constitution I — inviolable)\n    98\t\n    99\tNumbers reach the page only through `{{measure}}`. `kpi_card.value` and `driver_row` box\n   100\t`val` must contain a token; `insight.html`, `subtitle.text`, kpi `sub` and `delta.text` are","duration_ms":0}}

