data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01TXSiuv1VDNzfubmQQK1oWA","output":"   101\tscanned for formatted numbers (`9.972,6`, `+1,6%`, `79.490`) sitting outside one. A\n   102\theadline that isn't summable from fact rows is a `const` measure — still bound by a token.\n   103\t\n   104\t```\n   105\t// WRONG — the numbers are typed:\n   106\t\"sub\": \"Đạt: 101,6% · +9,2% vs Budget\"\n   107\t\n   108\t// RIGHT — every number is a measure reference:\n   109\t\"measures\": { \"toi_ach_total\": {\"expr\": \"toi_act / toi_bud * 100\", \"format\": \"pct1\"},\n   110\t              \"nii_vs_bud_pct\": {\"expr\": \"(nii_act - nii_bud) / nii_bud * 100\", \"format\": \"pct1\"} }\n   111\t\"sub\": \"Đạt: {{toi_ach_total|pct1}} · {{nii_vs_bud_pct|pct1}} vs Budget\"\n   112\t```\n   113\t\n   114\tNever invent a literal, never rescale (`/1000`, `*100`), never modify sub-agent SQL or data.\n   115\tThis is why one figure cannot appear two ways in one report.\n   116\t\n   117\t## Blocks\n   118\t\n   119\t`insight` (prose) · `subtitle` · `kpi_group` · `driver_row` · `chart` · `chart_pair` ·\n   120\t`table` · `actions` · `divider`. `{{measure}}` or `{{measure|format}}` works anywhere text\n   121\tis shown; `<strong>`/`<em>` survive in prose, everything else is escaped.\n   122\t\n   123\t**`table`** is always click-to-sort and filter-aware. Pick exactly one row mode:\n   124\tfact-driven (`fact` + `columns:[{col,label,align,format,cf}]`, rows auto-generate — prefer\n   125\tthis for detail tables) or explicit (`rows:[{key,cells}]`). Add `dim` to make rows hide\n   126\tunder a slicer, and `total:{cells:[…]}` with tokens for a footer that recomputes.\n   127\t\n   128\t**Charts always bind a fact** — there is no inline `values`/`categories` mode, because\n   129\tclick-to-filter needs a real column to key the slicer on.\n   130\t\n   131\t- `bar_group` / `line` — `x: {from_fact, col}` + `series: [{name, from: {fact, col, agg?}}]`.\n   132\t- `pie` — `slices: {from_fact, name_col, value_col}`.\n   133\t- `afb_line` — Actual/Forecast/Budget by month. **Its shape differs from `bar_group`/`line`:**\n   134\t  top-level `months` plus three sibling objects, matched to `months` by row order.\n   135\t  ```json\n   136\t  { \"kind\": \"afb_line\",\n   137\t    \"months\": [\"T1\", \"T2\", \"T3\", \"T4\", \"T5\", \"T6\"],\n   138\t    \"actual\":   { \"from\": { \"fact\": \"toi_afb\", \"col\": \"actual\" } },\n   139\t    \"forecast\": { \"from\": { \"fact\": \"toi_afb\", \"col\": \"forecast\" } },\n   140\t    \"budget\":   { \"from\": { \"fact\": \"toi_afb\", \"col\": \"budget\" } },\n   141\t    \"forecast_band\": [\"T4\", \"T6\"] }\n   142\t  ```\n   143\t  `toi_afb` has one row per month (`actual` null past the cutover, `forecast` null before).\n   144\t  All three of `actual`/`forecast`/`budget` are required.\n   145\t\n   146\tShape limits the schema enforces: `kpi_group.columns` ∈ {2,3} (no 4-column CSS — split into\n   147\ta second group) · `chart_pair` holds exactly 2 charts · `driver_row` ≤ 4 boxes · `actions`\n   148\tpriority ∈ {high, medium} · `progress` takes `width` **or** `ratio` · ids match\n   149\t`^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$`.\n   150\t\n   151\t## Filters & conditional formats\n   152\t\n   153\t`filters: [ { \"dim\": \"sector\" } ]` builds the slicer and turns on chart cross-filtering.\n   154\t**A chart axis or pie slice bound to a declared dimension needs that dimension in\n   155\t`filters[]`** — without slicer state to toggle, the click would silently do nothing, so the\n   156\tlint rejects it. (If the axis isn't meant to be interactive, don't bind it to a dimension.)\n   157\t\n   158\t`conditional_formats` maps values to RAG classes, referenced by name from a KPI `cf`,\n   159\tprogress `rule`, or cell `cf`:\n   160\t\n   161\t```json\n   162\t{ \"thresholds\": [ {\"op\":\"lt\",\"value\":85,\"class\":\"bad\"}, {\"op\":\"lt\",\"value\":100,\"class\":\"warn\"} ],\n   163\t  \"else_class\": \"good\" }\n   164\t```\n   165\t\n   166\t`op: \"between\"` also needs `value2`.\n   167\t\n   168\t### Cross-filtering across breakdowns\n   169\t\n   170\tA slicer only reaches a fact whose rows carry that dimension's column, so two breakdowns\n   171\tco-filter only through a shared column. In order of preference:\n   172\t\n   173\t1. **One fact at the intersection grain.** Ask Genie for the metric broken down by *both*\n   174\t   dims in a single query and emit one fact. Every measure aggregates from it, both slicers\n   175\t   cross-filter everything, and totals reconcile.\n   176\t2. **Stamp the parent key** when grains differ but a hierarchy exists (product → segment):\n   177\t   add the parent key to each child row, and picking a `sector` narrows the product fact.\n   178\t   The reverse stays undone on purpose — a segment total can't be re-derived from one\n   179\t   product without product-grain data.\n   180\t3. **Keep them independent and say so.** Two disjoint facts are two honest lenses. Note it\n   181\t   rather than invent an intersection Genie never returned.\n   182\t\n   183\tModel at the grain you want filtered and ask Genie for that grain. Never synthesize the\n   184\tintersection in the config.\n   185\t\n   186\t## Sections\n   187\t\n   188\tA section's `label` is both the eyebrow above its H2 and its sidebar link — one source, no\n   189\t`nav` field. `in_nav:false` hides a section; `nav_level:1` nests it.","duration_ms":0}}

