data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01T2pdF1deq1v5KPk9rMMSHP","output":"     1\t# CIBG Customer Segmentation\n     2\t\n     3\t## Metadata\n     4\t- Domain: cibg\n     5\t- Category: customers\n     6\t- Tags: segmentation, segment, persona, archetype, active-customer, enterprise-type\n     7\t- Last updated: 2026-05-15\n     8\t- Source: D1_Business_Rules-Metrics__CIBG_CUSTOMER.md, D1_Business_Rules-Metrics__Define_segment_Sector_Persona__Data Dictionary cibg d cusinfo.md\n     9\t\n    10\t## Summary\n    11\tCIBG classifies corporate customers along 6 key dimensions: Segment (LC/MM/USME/SME), Area (North/South), Sector (5 focus + 2 special), Industry (GSO-based), CBC hierarchy (lv1/lv2), and Persona (behavioral archetypes). Segmentation is primarily driven by T24 SectorID classification and revenue thresholds.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Detail\n    14\t\n    15\t### 1. Segment Hierarchy\n    16\t\n    17\tThe primary segmentation dimension classifies customers by size/type:\n    18\t\n    19\t| Segment | Definition | Revenue Threshold | Classification Basis |\n    20\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n    21\t| **VVIP** | Very high TOI, deep relationship with TCB | N/A (relationship-based) | CBC_lv2 mapping (VVIP1,3,5,5A,5B,6) |\n    22\t| **LC** (Large Corporate) | Big size customers | Revenue > 2,000 bn VND | SectorID in (BIG, MMD, Treas) |\n    23\t| **MM** (Mid Market) | Medium-large customers | Revenue 200–2,000 bn VND | Within MMU, not SME |\n    24\t| **USME** (Upper SME) | Upper small-medium enterprises | Part of MMU segment | Within MMU, not SME |\n    25\t| **SME** (Small-Medium Enterprise) | Smaller enterprises | Part of MMU segment | Specific SectorID classification |\n    26\t| **Others** | Special/shared IDs | N/A | Special IDs (-1, -2, etc.) or shared accounting IDs |\n    27\t\n    28\t**Hierarchy levels:**\n    29\t\n    30\t```\n    31\tsegment_group (LC | MMU | Others)\n    32\t  └─ segment_group_lv2 (LC | MMU | SME)\n    33\t      └─ segment (LC | MM | USME | SME | Others)\n    34\t```\n    35\t\n    36\t**Classification logic:**\n    37\t- `segment_group`: LC = SectorID in (BIG, MMD, Treas); MMU = remaining; Others = special/shared IDs\n    38\t- `segment_group_lv2`: Same as segment_group but splits MMU into MMU + SME\n    39\t- `segment`: Most granular — splits MMU further into MM and USME\n    40\t\n    41\t### 2. Area (Geographic)\n    42\t\n    43\t| Area | Description |\n    44\t| --- | --- |\n    45\t| **North** | Customers based in North region |\n    46\t| **South** | Customers based in South region |\n    47\t| **FI** | Financial Institution customers (not area-based) |\n    48\t| **VVIPs** | VVIP customers (not area-based) |\n    49\t| **Others** | Special/shared IDs (not area-based) |\n    50\t\n    51\tArea is determined by the CBC managing the customer (`cbc_area` field).\n    52\t\n    53\t### 3. Sector Classification\n    54\t\n    55\tEconomic sectors mapped via **GSO_ID** (General Statistics Office code):\n    56\t\n    57\t| Type | Sectors | Notes |\n    58\t| --- | --- | --- |\n    59\t| **Focus sectors** (5) | Real Estate, Infrastructure, Healthcare, Entertainment_Travel_Hospitality, Financial Services | Strategic priority — see [[cibg-sector-strategy]] |\n    60\t| **Special: General ID** | Accounting/allocation purpose | Skip for business analysis |\n    61\t| **Special: Diversified Sector** | Groups unfocused sectors | Large customer count, mixed industries |\n    62\t\n    63\t**Sector hierarchy:**\n    64\t```\n    65\tsector (top level, e.g. \"Real Estate\")\n    66\t  └─ sub_sector (e.g. \"Construction\")\n    67\t      └─ sub_segment_gso / industry (e.g. \"Automotive spare parts commercialization\")\n    68\t```\n    69\t\n    70\t**Mapping priority:** GSO retag > GSO on T24 > Special customer mapping table\n    71\t\n    72\t### 4. Enterprise Type\n    73\t\n    74\t| Type | Definition |\n    75\t| --- | --- |\n    76\t| **SOE** | State-Owned Enterprise (sở hữu nhà nước) |\n    77\t| **FDI** | Foreign Direct Investment |\n    78\t| **PRI** | Private (remaining) |\n    79\t\n    80\t**FDI sub-classification:** DDI (Domestic Direct Investment) vs FDI (Foreign)\n    81\t\n    82\t### 5. Import/Export Classification\n    83\t\n    84\t| Category | Rule |\n    85\t| --- | --- |\n    86\t| **IMEX** | Has BOTH import AND export activity |\n    87\t| **IMPORT** | Has import activity only (not IMEX) |\n    88\t| **EXPORT** | Has export activity only (not IMEX) |\n    89\t| **DOMESTIC** | No import/export activity |\n    90\t\n    91\tActivity indicators: Import_USD, Vol_ImpLC_USD, Vol_TTR_Outward_USD, Customer purchasing FX (for import side); Export_USD, Vol_ExpLC_USD, Customer sell FX (for export side).\n    92\t\n    93\t### 6. Persona Logic\n    94\t\n    95\tPersona definition varies by segment:\n    96\t\n    97\t#### LC / MM / USME:\n    98\t```\n    99\tPersona = \"{segment_TCB}\" – \"{FDI}\" & \"{country_group_en_L2}\"\n   100\t```","duration_ms":0}}

