data: {"type":"response.output_item.done","item":{"type":"function_call_output","call_id":"toolu_bdrk_01HmvAcZ16SNNAAgWhSRnJ7s","output":"     1\t# CIBG Product Interpretation Framework\n     2\t\n     3\t## Metadata\n     4\t- Domain: cibg\n     5\t- Category: products\n     6\t- Tags: product-framework, interpretation, CASA, TD, lending, FX, trade-service, commentary\n     7\t- Last updated: 2026-06-19\n     8\t- Source: D1_Business_Rules-Metrics__CIBG_PRODUCTS.md\n     9\t\n    10\t## Summary\n    11\tA structured framework for interpreting CIBG product performance in business-finance analysis. For each product, defines the analytical lens: what it is, key metrics, core drivers, common distortions, and interpretation rules. Includes cross-product rules to prevent misleading conclusions.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Detail\n    14\t\n    15\t### How to Use This Framework\n    16\t\n    17\tFor each product, the analyst should understand:\n    18\t1. **Definition** — what the product represents commercially\n    19\t2. **Primary metrics** — which KPIs assess performance\n    20\t3. **Core business drivers** — what causes growth, decline, or volatility\n    21\t4. **Common distortions** — what creates misleading short-term movements\n    22\t5. **How to interpret changes** — what questions to ask before concluding\n    23\t6. **Common analytical cuts** — which dimensions are most useful\n    24\t\n    25\t### Universal Driver Framework\n    26\t\n    27\tAll CIBG products share a common set of core drivers:\n    28\t\n    29\t| Driver | Deposit/Lending products | Other products (FX, Trade Service) |\n    30\t| --- | --- | --- |\n    31\t| Penetration (%) | % khách hàng sử dụng sản phẩm trên tổng khách hàng | % khách hàng sử dụng sản phẩm trên tổng khách hàng |\n    32\t| Holding cus | Số lượng khách hàng đang nắm giữ sản phẩm | Số lượng khách hàng đang nắm giữ sản phẩm |\n    33\t| Avg bal / Avg val | Số dư bình quân (Avg bal) | Giá trị giao dịch bình quân (Avg val) |\n    34\t| %Margin | Biên lợi nhuận trên sản phẩm | Biên lợi nhuận trên sản phẩm |\n    35\t\n    36\t> **Decomposition logic:** Revenue = Holding cus × Avg bal (or val) × %Margin. Penetration drives Holding cus growth.\n    37\t\n    38\t---\n    39\t\n    40\t### 1. CASA (Current Account & Savings Account)\n    41\t\n    42\t**Definition:** Low-cost deposit balances in current/savings accounts. Treated as a balance product and key funding/relationship indicator.\n    43\t\n    44\t**Why it matters:**\n    45\t- Supports low-cost funding\n    46\t- Reflects transaction banking engagement\n    47\t- Signals relationship depth and cash management quality\n    48\t- Materially affects funding mix and margin economics\n    49\t\n    50\t**Primary metrics:** EOP bal, Avg bal, Net increase/decrease, Growth rate (MoM/QoQ/YoY), CASA share within total deposits, NTB vs existing-book CASA (by custype)\n    51\t\n    52\t**Core drivers:**\n    53\t- Penetration (%) — tỷ lệ khách hàng CIBG có CASA trên tổng khách hàng\n    54\t- Holding cus — số lượng khách hàng đang giữ CASA\n    55\t- Avg bal — số dư bình quân mỗi khách hàng\n    56\t- %Margin — biên lợi nhuận từ CASA (funding cost advantage)\n    57\t\n    58\t**Common distortions:**\n    59\t- Temporary cash parking near period-end\n    60\t- One-off inflows from project milestones\n    61\t- Large short-lived balances from concentrated clients\n    62\t- Month-end treasury/settlement timing effects\n    63\t- Operational delays in outflows or internal transfers\n    64\t\n    65\t**Interpretation checklist:**\n    66\t- Was the movement broad-based or concentrated in a few customers?\n    67\t- Is the change structural or temporary timing effect?\n    68\t- Did uplift come from existing customers or new business?\n    69\t- Is the balance linked to a known pipeline event or one-off deal?\n    70\t- Does average balance tell a different story from EOP balance?\n    71\t\n    72\t**Useful analytical cuts:** segment_group_cbc / segment, Sector / industry, custype (Existing vs New), area / cbc_lv1 / cbc_lv2\n    73\t\n    74\t> **Caution:** Do not treat all CASA growth as equally valuable. Sustainable operational CASA is more meaningful than short-lived concentration-driven balances.\n    75\t\n    76\t---\n    77\t\n    78\t### 2. TD (Term Deposit)\n    79\t\n    80\t**Definition:** Time-bound deposit balances placed for a defined tenor, usually at higher funding cost than CASA.\n    81\t\n    82\t**Why it matters:**\n    83\t- Important funding volume source\n    84\t- Supports balance-sheet growth or liquidity objectives\n    85\t- More rate-sensitive than CASA\n    86\t\n    87\t**Primary metrics:** EOP bal, Avg bal, Net increase/decrease, Cost of funds / implied pricing, Mix by tenor, Mix by customer segment\n    88\t\n    89\t**Core drivers:**\n    90\t- Penetration (%) — tỷ lệ khách hàng CIBG có TD trên tổng khách hàng\n    91\t- Holding cus — số lượng khách hàng đang giữ TD\n    92\t- Avg bal — số dư bình quân mỗi khách hàng\n    93\t- %Margin — biên lợi nhuận từ TD (spread giữa lending yield và cost of TD)\n    94\t\n    95\t**Interpretation checklist:**\n    96\t- Was growth price-led or relationship-led?\n    97\t- Did balances come from new money or internal migration from CASA?\n    98\t- Is the increase sustainable after campaign expiry?\n    99\t- Are shorter-tenor balances driving volatility?\n   100\t","duration_ms":0}}

